WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.940
There are a small number of gutsy Hollywood
stars who insist on doing their own stunt

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:04.440
work.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.760
But because most A-listers are happy to hand
the really dangerous stuff over to the professionals,

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.560
stunt doubles are always in demand in Tinseltown.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.300
Unfortunately, not every stunt has a happy
ending.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:18.460
Brushes with death are an occupational hazard
for Hollywood stunt doubles — and these

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:19.800
were some of the most hazardous.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:22.200
Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows - Part
1

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:27.160
Warner Bros. tried to use practical effects
whenever possible in their Harry Potter series,

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.720
especially when it came to broomsticks.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.980
That didn't mean the studio was happy to put
its star witches and wizards on those broomsticks,

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:33.480
however.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.580
Stuntman David Holmes doubled for Daniel Radcliffe
in many scenes, all the way back to the first

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:38.080
film.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:41.860
During Deathly Hallows Part 1, Holmes was
filming a flying stunt when he was yanked

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:45.220
from his broom and slammed into a wall before
falling to the ground.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:49.190
The accident broke his neck and left him paralyzed
at the age of 25.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:49.980
Holmes told The Mirror,

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:53.960
"I remember slipping in and out of consciousness
because of the pain levels."

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:55.880
"I knew I had really done some damage."

00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:00.239
Radcliffe himself thinks of Holmes as a friend
rather than a colleague, and hosted a charity

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.480
auction to help Holmes pay for his medical
bills.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.260
Back to the Future Part II

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:08.420
The hoverboard scene is one of the most memorable
moments from Back to the Future Part II, though

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:13.070
for stunt performer Cheryl Wheeler, it brings
back painful memories, since she was almost

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:14.300
killed shooting the sequence.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:19.640
"arrrrrgh!"

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:26.780
One stuntwoman had already quit over the scene,
and Wheeler became concerned after a handful

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:28.700
of last-minute changes were made to the rig.

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:32.240
After being accused of getting cold feet,
the stunt coordinator threatened to put a

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:34.620
male stunt performer in her clothes for the
scene.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:38.800
Being new to the business and wanting to make
an impression, she reluctantly agreed.

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:42.970
Instead of crashing through the sugar glass
window, Wheeler collided with a stone pillar

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:47.360
and was dropped 30 feet onto the concrete
below, missing the fall mats entirely.

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:50.940
Fellow stunt performer Gary Morgan recalled
in the book We Don't Need Roads,

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:55.040
"I got up and Cheryl was laying on the concrete
and the pool of blood by her head was getting

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.040
bigger.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:56.680
I thought she was dead."

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.960
Fortunately, Cheryl was quickly back in action,
and is still performing stunts as recently

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:01.920
as 2015.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.640
The Expendables 2

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:08.100
Countless henchmen are maimed and killed during
the many explosions that take place throughout

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:12.240
Sylvester Stallone's Expendables films, though
one of them actually claimed a life for real.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:16.720
Stuntman Kun Lieu was fatally injured during
the filming of a scene in Bulgaria involving

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.060
an inflatable raft for The Expendables 2.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:23.080
While Lieu's life could not be saved, his
partner during the stunt, Nuo Sun, somehow

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.200
escaped with his.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:29.540
According to court papers, Sun sustained damage
to his "nervous system, neck, head, body [and]

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:33.320
arms," which left him in "great mental, physical
and nervous pain and suffering."

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:38.100
The stunt performer sued Millennium Films
for $25,000 as well as the cost of his lengthy

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.720
hospital treatment and recovery.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.620
Today, Sun continues to work in the stunt
department of films like Ant-Man and Logan.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:45.840
Resident Evil: The Final Chapter

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:49.980
Star Milla Jovovich said that it was a "miracle"
her double survived an incident that took

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:55.350
place on the set of 2016's Resident Evil:
The Final Chapter, which left a British stuntwoman

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:55.850
in a coma.

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:57.920
According to a Facebook post by Jovovich,

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:02.700
"My incredibly talented stunt double, Olivia
Jackson, collided with a camera crane while

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:07.420
performing a motorcycle stunt and it put her
in the hospital with severe, multiple injuries."

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:11.700
After she regained consciousness, Jackson
also took to Facebook to reveal the horrifying

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:16.990
extent of the damage, which included a degloved
face, brain swelling, an amputated thumb,

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.660
and a missing piece of bone.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.940
She called the incident, quote, "not her funnest
day on set".

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.640
In the end, one of Jackson's arms had to be
amputated.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:29.040
The resilient Brit posted a picture of her
"twisted upper body" to her Instagram feed

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.460
in January 2017, claiming that her off-centered
neck is the most painful part, saying,

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:37.110
"I don't mean to moan, but sometimes I just
want to crawl out of my own skin and all the

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:37.880
pains in it."

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:41.340
For what it's worth, she seems to be keeping
in good spirits about her injuries.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:42.980
The Hangover Part II

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:47.900
Australian stuntman Scott McLean was doubling
for funnyman Ed Helms in The Hangover Part

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:52.420
2 when the stunt drivers involved in the film's
car chase reportedly got their marks wrong,

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:54.060
and McLean's head was hit by a truck.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:58.380
He suffered a critical head injury, forcing
hospital staff to put him in a medically induced

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:58.880
coma.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:03.520
McLean was feared dead by his colleagues after
the impact, and while he ultimately escaped

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:07.040
with his life, his lawyers claim he suffered
permanent brain injuries.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.380
His wife commented,

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:09.440
"There was so much damage.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:10.320
He was a mess.

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:13.680
He used to look after me, now it's my turn
to look after him for a change."

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:18.540
McLean's life will never be the same despite
extensive therapy, but today, he speaks openly

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.360
and positively about his recovery.

